{
  "abstract": "The freely generated zero-identity Boolean category of Došen and Petrić is maximal: every congruence preserved by the proof operations and uniform substitution is either equality or identifies every pair of parallel arrows. The Lean development constructs the equation-generated category and proves cut elimination and Boolean coherence, then proves maximality through both a symmetric-fold argument and the manuscript's short argument using two particular isomorphisms. It also formalizes the model corollary and the occurrence-substitution, finite-ordinal and structural-diagram constructions in the appendices. The registry selection compares the two maximality proofs, the congruence dichotomy, a nonzero literal identity and the absence of arrows from the terminal object to the initial object.",
